  slug: 'uganda-vs-rwanda-gorillas',
  kicker: 'A side-by-side comparison',
  heroImg: '/images/gorillas/gorilla-mother-infant-closeup.jpg',
  heroImgAlt: 'Mountain gorilla mother holding infant in Bwindi Impenetrable Forest Uganda',
  description: 'Uganda vs Rwanda gorilla trekking: honest side-by-side comparison of permit costs, number of gorilla families, trek difficulty, lodges, and which country suits your budget and travel style.',
  readTime: '6 min read',
  breadcrumb: 'Uganda vs Rwanda for Gorillas',
  intro: [
    'Both Uganda and Rwanda offer extraordinary gorilla trekking experiences. Mountain gorillas exist only in the Virunga Massif volcanic mountain range (shared by Uganda, Rwanda and DRC) and in Uganda\'s Bwindi Impenetrable Forest. The decision between the two countries comes down to budget, available time, the type of experience you want, and what else you want to combine with your trek.',
    'This guide gives you an honest, direct comparison of the two destinations across every important factor.',
  ],
